{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}ChatGPT — UCESCO Volunteer Manager{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6">
        <a href="{{ path('connect_ai_index') }}" class="inline-block text-sm text-slate-600 hover:underline">← Connect an AI</a>

        <div>
            <h1 class="text-xl font-semibold">ChatGPT</h1>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600"><twig:Pill tone="neutral">Not available yet</twig:Pill></p>
        </div>

        <section class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
            <h2 id="why-heading" class="font-semibold">Why it isn't available</h2>
            <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-slate-700">
                <li>
                    <strong>UCESCO agreed to Claude, not to OpenAI.</strong> Each company that receives volunteers'
                    data has to be agreed separately, with its own terms and data protection basis.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>It needs a paid workspace.</strong> Connecting a custom server to ChatGPT takes a Business or
                    Enterprise workspace, with developer mode turned on by its admin.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Mikono would need changes.</strong> ChatGPT signs in differently from Claude, so it can't
                    connect today, even if you try.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">If UCESCO wants this, ask whoever maintains Mikono.</p>
        </section>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
